DCS 1
cast BRICKS
# Brick Realm (REALM-CASTS.md): baseplates, studs for money, blueprints for quests.

who Foreman Kip
voice 4 1.0
step start
if bridge_done -> tower
if bridge -> waiting
say Builder! The river plate's got no bridge and the Twins won't swim.
ask Build the bridge? Blueprint's yours. | On it=accept | Not yet=later
step accept
set bridge
give PLAN_BRIDGE 1
say Red bricks, forty of them, and a grey plate for the deck. Snap them on the line; the plan shows where.
end
step later
say The river's not going anywhere. The Twins might.
end
step waiting
ask Bridge up? | Not yet=hint | It's up=done
step hint
say Count your reds. Forty. The Baker's got more if you're short.
end
step done
set bridge_done
say She holds! Next: a tower. Forty studs tall. The Archivist has the plan.
end
step tower
say Tower next. Forty studs. Don't lean it; Bloom's cousin rates these.
end

who Brick Baker
voice 2 0.9
step start
say Reds by the thousand. Blues when the kiln's hot. Clear ones once a week, if the glass holds.
ask Buying? | Red=red | Blue=blue | Clear=clear
step red
say Ten for a stud. Take a hundred; everyone runs short of red.
end
step blue
say Three for a stud. Kiln's hot today, you're lucky.
end
step clear
say One, and it's a stud a piece. The Collector would trade you a realm for it.
end

who Blueprint Archivist
voice 6 0.85
step start
if bridge_done -> tower_plan
say Every design ever snapped is in here. Most of them twice. Bring me a plan and I'll file it; ask and I'll find one.
ask Find a plan? | A bridge=bridge | A tower=locked | Nothing=no
step bridge
say Bridge, forty reds, one grey deck. Kip's favourite. Here.
end
step locked
say Tower's behind the bridge, builder. Rules of the library.
end
step no
say The shelves will wait. They are shelves.
end
step tower_plan
set tower_plan
give PLAN_TOWER 1
say The bridge is up? Then the tower plan is yours. Forty studs, and the top brick is clear, if you have one.
end

who Crane Operator Sal
voice 1 0.8
step start
say Built something in the wrong place? Sal lifts it. Whole. Don't ask how.
ask Move a build? | Yes=move | Not now=no
step move
say Point at it. ...There. Mind your head; it's coming over.
end
step no
say Sal waits. Sal has a crane.
end

who Demolition Duo
voice 10 1.2
step start
say WE KNOCK THINGS DOWN. Race you to the old wall: first to flatten it wins a plate.
ask Race? | GO=race | Not today=no
step race
set race
say THREE TWO ONE... (They are already gone.)
end
step no
say Coward's a strong word. We'll use it anyway.
end

who Mayor Minifold
voice 8 1.05
step start
say Citizen! The city needs a yellow district. Yellow bricks, yellow plates, yellow everything. For morale.
ask Help the Mayor? | For morale=yes | That's a lot of yellow=no
step yes
set yellow
say Excellent. The hat approves. The hat is most of me.
end
step no
say The hat has noted your name.
end

who Airfield Ace Nova
voice 7 1.1
step start
if prop -> ready
say Your plane's prop is stock. Stock loses laps. I've got one that doesn't.
ask Fit the racing prop? | Fit it=fit | Keep stock=no
step fit
set prop
give PLANE_PROP 1
say Fitted. Three laps of the runway, then we talk about the Cup.
end
step no
say Stock's fine for sightseeing.
end
step ready
say Prop's spinning sweet. The Cup's Sunday.
end

who Toy Soldier Sergeant
voice 0 0.75
step start
say SQUAD. Four of you, one of me. Formation is a shape. Hold the shape and nothing gets through.
ask Drill? | Yes, Sergeant=drill | Later, Sergeant=no
step drill
set drilled
say WEDGE. LINE. BOX. Again. ...Not bad. You'll do.
end
step no
say Dismissed. Temporarily.
end

who Missing-Piece Collector
voice 9 0.95
step start
say One rare brick from every realm. That's the set. I've got four. There are more realms than four.
ask Got one for me? | A clear brick=clear | Not yet=no
step clear
set collector_clear
say A clear! From here? That counts. Five. Bring me a mural piece from the city of frames next.
end
step no
say The set waits. Sets are patient. Collectors aren't.
end

who Glue Witch
voice 11 0.8
step start
say Snap it, and it comes apart. Glue it, and it never does. Never is the price.
ask Buy glue? | One pot=pot | Never's too long=no
step pot
give GLUE_POT 1
say One pot. Use it on something you're sure of. Nobody ever is.
end
step no
say Wise. Or scared. The glue doesn't care which.
end

who Studmonger
voice 3 1.0
step start
say Studs in, studs out. Pigment, honey, chalk: I'll change any of it, at a rate you won't like.
ask Exchange? | Pigment to studs=pigment | Studs to honey=honey | No=no
step pigment
say Two studs a pigment. Red. Blue's four. Gold, we'll talk.
end
step honey
say A jar for ten studs. The bees are far and the Crow takes a cut.
end
step no
say The rate was better yesterday. It always was.
end

who Builder Kids Club
voice 5 1.15
step start
say Our fort's got a secret room! You'll never find it! ...It's behind the blue bricks. Don't tell the others.
ask Look for the secret? | I'll find it=yes | I won't tell=no
step yes
set fort_secret
say You found it! Okay you're in the club. Rule one: no grown-ups. Rule two: more bricks.
end
step no
say Good. Rule one: no telling.
end
